    {
      "id": "claim_6e4e02e4ac364e1abb17453cae95ad2c",
      "statement": "admitRuntime() admits a dispatch only when the requested executor kind holds an evidence-backed RUNTIME_ADMISSIONS record (decision ADMIT, CONDITIONAL, or unexpired LEGACY_ADMITTED; a critical-gate FAIL can never be outweighed) correlated with the binary version the contract probe observed since this process booted — never task metadata or runtime output; every decision is persisted as an execution event with the assessment ref, denials also record a runtime_admission policy violation, and RUNTIME_ADMISSION_MODE=shadow records the denial but lets the run proceed.",
