      "statement": "recoverInterruptedTasks() runs once at server boot (index.ts L213-L216) and reconciles tasks left durable-running: only a task whose reserved execution_recovery_attempt stamp matches the latest engine-authored admitted event on event_id and attempt_id and confirms an unsandboxed in-process mock is failed as interrupted_in_process; everything else (unknown, malformed, forged, real/fallback/sandboxed attempts) becomes paused with execution_recovery_hold: true and outcome unknown — recovery never replays work, never kills PIDs, never clears an uncertain hold, writes the recovery event/audit/evidence in one transaction, and is idempotent.",
